# What the daemon receives is this file's business, not an afterthought: bin/ alone is 563 MB of local publish
# output in this working tree, and .git is the whole history. Neither is an input to anything the image builds,
# and shipping them makes every build slow for no gain.
#
# Excluding them is also what keeps the image honest about what it builds FROM: the image is built from
# committed sources, never from whatever happens to be lying in the working tree. A stale local publish output
# can therefore not leak into a release artefact. docs/build-image.md is the document for all of this.

# Version control and editor/agent state.
.git
.gitattributes
.idea
.claude
*.DotSettings.user

# Local build output (both TFMs, the RID-specific publish folders, and the test runner's own droppings).
**/bin
**/obj
**/TestResults
publish
publish-linux
dist

# Driver build output. The driver image unpacks its own tools, and the driver stage COPYs the five files
# build.sh reads and nothing else — so the locally built .sys/.pdb and the extracted signtool.exe are dead
# weight here. (`driver/**/out` is git-ignored, so it is only ever present on a machine that has built it.)
driver/**/out
driver/**/x64
driver/**/tools
